5zZTU="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["alignment","data-analysis","data-science","flexible","pandas","python"],"visibility":"public","forks":19393,"open_issues":3594,"watchers":47298,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"I've had recently made the experience of implementing and maintaining different down-stream applications supporting or building upon pandas. One thing I've learned is that it's quite painful to write code that e.g. runs for pandas 0.7.3 up to current master. Although 0.7.3 seems rather old given the rapid dev-cycle and the vibrant community, one may not forget that 0.7.3 is not older than 1.5 - 2 years and hence still counts as stable version in quite a few distros (while user-studies show that many people, let alone institutions, are often years behind recent versions ...).\nWhich guidelines to follow to make life easier when supporting such use cases does not seem too well documented. What would people think about adding such a -- maybe growing -- collection of hints + tips to the docs?\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/5027/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/5027/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":2654595449,"node_id":"MDE1OlJlZmVyZW5jZWRFdmVudDI2NTQ1OTU0NDk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pandas-dev/pandas/issues/events/2654595449","actor":{"login":"dan-nadler","id":10131558,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTMxNTU4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10131558?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dan-nadler","html_url":"https://github.com/dan-nadler","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dan-nadler/followers","follo